& [DictatedObjective]
  + Git should and will have the whole authoritative SJS graph
  + every governed element must carry in its history the justification marks for what was done to it at every turn
  + commit comments should expose the element-specific justification produced by SJS while the repository stores the full traversable decision graph
  + resume Cantor work for a six-hour slice and advance the highest-leverage unblocked product seam

& [SelectedBoundedProduct]
  + form and implement Cantor SJS Repository Change-Set P0 as a provider-free safe Rust verification surface
  + model stable element identity typed SJS nodes typed edges per-turn element history events independent diff inventory exact path coverage and immutable correction history
  + expose a bounded verifier that accepts supplied strict machine forms and emits a verification-only receipt
  + preserve the full graph in repository-relative content and make commit narrative justification proof and frontier traversal mechanically checkable

& [RequiredDelineation]
  + inside are pure supplied-data validation deterministic canonical JSON domain-separated SHA256 strict parsing adversarial fixtures a read-only input-file CLI and checked evidence
  + boundary is independent staged-diff inventory supplied to the verifier rather than trusted claims embedded only in the change set
  + outside are Git process launch workspace mutation staging commit push history rewrite provider model network secrets chain of thought activation and foreign dirty work

& [Acceptance]
  + every supplied changed path is covered by at least one compatible element history event and every event path belongs to the supplied diff inventory
  + additions deletions modifications renames generated refreshes before and after identities and tombstones are validated exactly
  + graph node and edge references element identities event identities content digests commit bookends and foreign exclusions are bounded unique and strict
  + successful verification is deterministic replayable physical_contact false and authority verification_only
  + malformed traversal duplicates missing coverage authority widening unknown fields digest drift and resource overflow are refused

& [Nonclaims]
  + P0 does not prove that the supplied inventory came from Git or that a commit was created published trusted or immutable
  + P0 does not grant write commit push activation provider or self-signature authority
  + physical staged-diff capture and commit-hook enforcement require separately governed integration after the pure verifier exists
